<title>NIGERIA: Elf says Nigerian oil output not hit by protests.</title>
<headline>Elf says Nigerian oil output not hit by protests.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elf Petroleum Nigeria Ltd said on Thursday its operations were going on normally and had not been affected by community disturbances in oil-producing areas of Nigeria.</p>
<p>&quot;We operate in the Delta but our location is a bit far from where this problem is going on and our own production has not been affected,&quot; said a company spokesman in Lagos.</p>
<p>Elf Nigeria pumps 130,000 barrels per day of crude oil, a fraction of the production of Royal Dutch Shell Group, which is losing 210,000 bpd because villagers have occupied seven of its flow stations in protests over changes to their local government areas.</p>
<p>-- Lagos newsroom +234 1 2630317</p>
